    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present this exceptionally finished, detached family residence to the market.\nBoasting a bright, spacious interior and a high-specification finish throughout, this impressive five-bedroom home exudes style and quality in every detail. Thoughtfully designed to meet the demands of modern family living, the property features a beautifully crafted bespoke kitchen, generous light-filled living spaces, and a directly south-facing rear garden.\n\nThe well-proportioned accommodation comprises an inviting entrance hallway, elegant living room, and a stunning open-plan family/kitchen/dining area. Additional features on the ground floor include a guest WC/utility room, a second kitchen room offering excellent potential for those requiring a self-contained or semi-independent living space, ideal for a parent, au pair, or extended family member, and three bedrooms. Upstairs, there are two spacious bedrooms, a family bathroom, and a large walk-in wardrobe room.\n\nTo the rear, the property benefits from a versatile garden room suitable for a variety of uses, a large wooden garden shed, and expansive outdoor areas ideal for family enjoyment. To the front, a private garden provides ample off-street parking.\n\nIdeally located on the highly sought-after Sundrive Road, the property is within easy walking distance of Rush town centre and its beautiful beaches. Rush is a charming seaside village, conveniently located near Skerries and Lusk, and within easy commuting distance of Dublin Airport and the City Centre. The area offers an excellent selection of schools, shops, restaurants, pubs, and recreational amenities, with The Mill Bank Theatre and the local national school just a few minutes' walk from the property.\n\nExcellent transport links include a regular and frequent bus service to Dublin City and surrounding areas, while Rush train station is just a five-minute drive away. The M1, M50, and Dublin Airport are all accessible within approximately 20 minutes."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nTiled floor to entrance, herringbone wood floor to hallway coving, recessed lights\n\nLiving Room - \nSolid oak floor, dual aspect, feature fireplace with stove insert, French sliding doors to rear garden\n\nKitchen / Dining / Family Room - \nTiled floor, bespoke fitted kitchen with wall and floor mounted units, tiled splash back, Siemens appliances - integrated double oven, hob & dishwasher, quartz countertops island unit with storage and seating area,Pantry Press with storage , Seating area with feature electric fireplace,Traditional vertical radiator,bay window with French door to garden.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nSpacious double room, carpet to floor, built in wardrobes, bay window\n\nBedroom 2 - \nSpacious double room, carpet to floor\n\nBedroom 3 - \nDouble room, carpet to floor\n\nKitchen / Family Room - \nWonderful spacious room, wood floor, fitted kitchen with wall and floor mounted units, tiled splashback, bay window, seating area\n\nEn-suite - \nTiled floor, WC, WHB, Shower unit\n\nGuest WC / Utility Room - \nTiled floor, WC, Vanity unit WHB, fitted units for storage with tiled splash back, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, window\n\nLanding - \nCarpet to floor, velux window, recessed lights\n\nMain Bedroom - \nCarpet to floor, spacious double room, Feature wall, eaves storage\n\nBathroom - \nTiled floor, free standing bath, shower unit with fully tiled walls and seating, wash hand basin vanity unit\n\nBedroom 5 - \nCarpet to floor, spacious room, home office area, access to walk in wardrobe\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - \nSpacious room, carpet to floor, hanging and shelving units\n\nRear Garden - \nSpacious gardens, South facing aspect, lawn, patio and decking areas, two side entrances, garden shed suitable for a number of uses, large wooden shed, walled boundaries\n\nFront Garden - \nDesigned with low mainteance in mind, off street parking, electric charging area, mature flower beds, two side entrances, solar panels\n\n"
      },
